# Director decision - first real app workflow
date: 2026-10-31
who: Codex Prime recording Director instruction
state: agreed direction; not runtime activation

## Director reply, verbatim
> Yes it should be. We want the compute to be building the faces and the pages. Once it's working.

## Decision and context
The first real workflow for the current Prime is reviewing one builder return:
discover returned work -> retrieve assignment, capture and evidence -> intelligent
inspection -> record Prime judgment -> show next action -> recover after restart.
The work book remains the durable record; indexes and views point to it.

Compute should construct the pages/faces needed for that workflow from structured
inputs and explicit templates, preserving original captured returns and unchanged
content. Models supply content, judgment and proposed changes. Formatting,
addresses, required fields and structural checks should not require the model to
regenerate entire documents. Existing release and approval boundaries still apply.

## Sequencing
First integrate a usable return-review loop for Prime. Then move construction of
its records/pages/faces into compute as part of that path. A universal builder for
every face type is not a prerequisite for the first usable loop. The exact minimum
construction capability and its acceptance checks belong in the reviewed design.
Test that records are correctly shaped, evidence remains linked and durable,
unexplained source loss is refused where applicable, and restart recovers state.
No claim that these capabilities are implemented yet.

## Current assignment
Clarification for 0519/05.01: prioritize this concrete Prime use case and identify
how compute will construct its records. No expansion of Claude's allowed writes
or production implementation authority. Grok implements separately released packs.
No changes to the active pack, pinned sources or captured history by this note.
